finding: e674b198 removes the fixture's hooks isolation: GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL/GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM do not prevent git init from copying executable hooks from an inherited GIT_TEMPLATE_DIR. Reproduced without editing the worktree: created a temporary template/hooks/pre-commit containing '#!/bin/sh\nexit 42\n', exported GIT_TEMPLATE_DIR to that template, and ran bun test ./scripts/changed-tests.node.ts -t 'non-ASCII'. The fixture fails at its commit (line 82), with an empty Error, before exercising non-ASCII selection. With the same template and a scratch git wrapper reinstating the removed '-c core.hooksPath=/dev/null', the test passes (3 assertions). A host template can also supply a prompting/hanging hook. Keep explicit hooks suppression or otherwise isolate templates; ignoring global/system configuration does not subsume this protection.
